{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_18-00-28-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nu={\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Read the retained receipt of experiment 0ac92aa98a744dfd93542a023d94f598 (CheckRun 3044e4e1ae284cf8abc323990e968c5c, exit 0, 34 events). Its event 33 records the negative control: after the same remove-and-re-add history, a snapshot taken once the widened configuration was committed carries five servers at index 20, and the node restarted from it recovers five servers matching the configuration in force. The account's statement of the trigger boundary is therefore measured in both directions.\\\",\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[\n  {\\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"680bc27c9c50448a8b63097d98091061-question-0\\\",\n   \\\"experiment_id\\\":\\\"680bc27c9c50448a8b63097d98091061-experiment\\\",\n   \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"s-scan\\\",\\\"s-restore-committed\\\",\\\"s-dispatch-stage\\\",\\\"s-appendentries-stage\\\",\\\"s-runfollower-gate\\\",\\\"s-config-doc\\\",\\\"s-commit-tracking-contract\\\",\\\"s-installsnapshot\\\"],\n   \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"5e1ce9aa430842d5a9325cfecbc885f6\\\":[0,1],\\\"e1ee764584564a95b3e288381dfb75d9\\\":[0,1],\\\"183f75213c5a4f26a951f76784b3e54f\\\":[15,16],\\\"5627b36f50384d14851e4b5da991fa96\\\":[30,31],\\\"e1f5bf19d9fa482380acf68d58ec197e\\\":[32],\\\"3044e4e1ae284cf8abc323990e968c5c\\\":[33]},\n   \\\"joint_history\\\":\\\"Six receipts of the same harness file answer this question. Two state the gap in clusters (5e1ce9aa430842d5a9325cfecbc885f6 and e1ee764584564a95b3e288381dfb75d9, each at its own indices 0 and 1), one states the gap for a hand-built history in a monotonic commit-tracking store (e1f5bf19d9fa482380acf68d58ec197e at index 32), one states the negative control where the snapshot already covers the change (3044e4e1ae284cf8abc323990e968c5c at index 33), and two state the repair paths (183f75213c5a4f26a951f76784b3e54f at 15 and 16, 5627b36f50384d14851e4b5da991fa96 at 30 and 31).\\\",\n   \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Current account: with RestoreCommittedLogs enabled a restarted node does not load the committed configuration entries at or below the commit index it recovers, the mechanism is store-independent, the trigger boundary is measured in both directions, and both repair paths are measured. Mechanism: restoreFromCommittedLogs clamps the store's commit index, applies the recovered range through processLogs (which ends with setLastApplied), and the scan then starts at max(lastSnapshotIndex, lastApplied)+1, so a configuration entry at or below that index never reaches processConfigurationLogEntry; the snapshot that restoreSnapshot loads is used as-is, which is why the outcome depends on whether that snapshot already covers the change. Evidence: 5e1ce9aa430842d5a9325cfecbc885f6 and e1ee764584564a95b3e288381dfb75d9 state the two shapes in clusters; e1f5bf19d9fa482380acf68d58ec197e states the same outcome for a directly written history in a monotonic commit-tracking store, with the applied index at the staged commit index and an empty recovered configuration; 3044e4e1ae284cf8abc323990e968c5c is the control, where the snapshot taken after the widening carries five servers at index 20 and the restarted node recovers five servers matching the configuration in force, so a cadence that snapshots past the change avoids the gap; 183f75213c5a4f26a951f76784b3e54f and 5627b36f50384d14851e4b5da991fa96 state the repairs. Consequences that remain source-derived rather than measured: runFollower refuses to campaign with no known peers, and quorumSize over an empty or stale voter list is wrong; the child questions measure what such a configuration admits, rejects and commits.\\\",\n   \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"violated\\\",\n   \\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\n   \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\n    \\\"The negative control shows the gap is conditional, not universal: when the node's snapshot already covers the change, the restart recovers the configuration in force.\\\",\n    \\\"Both repair paths are measured: an arriving configuration entry restores the full set while the node is still a member, and an installed snapshot restores it when log replication is impossible.\\\",\n    \\\"The gap reproduces for a commit-tracking store that is also marked monotonic, so it is not an artefact of the store's indexing shape.\\\",\n    \\\"No captured test asserts configuration state after a RestoreCommittedLogs restart, so the captured suite neither contradicts nor covers this path.\\\"\n   ],\n   \\\"limitations\\\":[\n    \\\"Applies to nodes configured with RestoreCommittedLogs=true and a LogStore implementing CommitTrackingLogStore; with the flag off, lastApplied equals the snapshot index and the scan range is unchanged.\\\",\n    \\\"All measurements use in-memory stores (including a hand-built monotonic commit-tracking store) with the repository's in-memory transport and mock FSM; production stores are not measured.\\\",\n    \\\"The installed-snapshot repair needed the leader's log to have been compacted past the node's last index, which the probe arranged by letting the cluster commit eighty entries while the node was down; other ways of reaching that state are not measured.\\\"\n   ]}\n ]\n}\njson.dump(u,open('update.json','w'),indent=2); print('written')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_18-00-28-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -2\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
